This product bootstraps from and adapts the following works:

1. pdfdrill (Wulf Kolbe)
   The deterministic semantic graph, the content-hash (blake2b) node identity, and
   the type-checking compiler philosophy in `src/codedrill/schema.py` are derived from
   pdfdrill's `src/semantic` package. `src/codedrill/pdfdrill_adapter.py` projects a
   codedrill graph into pdfdrill's `SemanticGraph` to reuse its compiler unchanged.

2. Understand-Anything — Egonex-AI (MIT License)
   https://github.com/Egonex-AI/Understand-Anything
   The knowledge-graph contract is adapted from
   understand-anything-plugin/packages/core/src/schema.ts, specifically:
     - the canonical node-type and edge-type vocabularies (NODE_TYPES / EDGE_TYPES),
     - the LLM-output alias-normalization tables (NODE_TYPE_ALIASES / EDGE_TYPE_ALIASES /
       COMPLEXITY_ALIASES) in `src/codedrill/schema.py`,
     - the layer-detector heuristic (API/Service/Data/UI/Utility) in `src/codedrill/context.py`,
     - the language-concept catalogue in `src/codedrill/concepts.py`,
   so that a codedrill `knowledge-graph.json` round-trips through Understand-Anything's
   dashboard and merge tooling unchanged.

